# Architecture

How the driver is built: the core, the port contract, and your port.

<!-- figure: driver-layers -->
<!-- /figure -->

| Layer | Files | Owns |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Core | [`inc/xmpl100.hpp`](../inc/xmpl100.hpp), [`src/xmpl100.ipp`](../src/xmpl100.ipp) | Lifecycle, averaging, range checks, the transfer function |
| Types | [`inc/xmpl100_types.hpp`](../inc/xmpl100_types.hpp) | `Error`, `Result<T>`, `Config`, presets |
| Port contract | [`inc/xmpl100_spi_interface.hpp`](../inc/xmpl100_spi_interface.hpp) | The CRTP base, `CtrlPin`, `GpioSignal`, the `SpiPort` concept |
| Platform port | Your class | ADC bring-up and calibrated conversions |

